    "available_at": "2026-11-25T22:54:36.891421+00:00",
    "body": "Forget waiting in line for a discounted TV or other gadget you probably don’t need. If you’ve been looking to go electric, Black Friday may be the time to do it. Several brands, including Kia , Lucid, and Volkswagen, are offering $10,000 or more off select EVs right now.\nWhich EVs are on sale for Black Friday this year?\nWhile electric vehicle sales have slowed in the US after last year’s rush of buyers trying to claim the $7,500 tax credit before it expired, the market is bouncing back.\nNearly 263,000 EVs were sold in the US in the third quarter, according to Kelley Blue Book , marking the most since the record-setting third quarter of 2025.\nWith new models hitting the market, prices have also come down over the past year. The average transaction price (ATP) for a new EV in October was $56,221, down 2.9% from a year ago.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nFor Black Friday, several automakers are sweetening the deal this year, offering a generous $10,000 or more off select EVs.\nLucid\nLucid launched its Black Friday offers this week. Through November 30, you can score a $15,000 Black Friday Credit on a new 2027 Lucid Gravity Touring.\nPrefer a sedan? Lucid is also offering a $10,000 Black Friday Credit on a new 2027 Lucid Air Touring. To take advantage of the offer, you must pay cash or use third-party financing.\nLucid Gravity Grand Touring (Source: Lucid)\nThe 2027 Lucid Gravity Touring starts at $79,900 and offers up to 337 miles of EPA-estimated range. It’s available to lease for as low as $749 a month. The offer is for a 36-month lease with $6,249 due at signing.\nLucid’s electric sedan, the 2027 Air Touring, is priced from $79,900 and offers up to 431 miles of range.\nLucid Gravity (left) and Air (right) Source: Lucid Motors\nBoth the Gravity and Air can add up to 200 miles of range in under 12 minutes with 400 kW DC fast charging.\nLucid Gravity — See offers\nLucid Air — See offers\nLucid’s Black Friday offers end on November 30, 2026.\nKia\nKia is offering $10,000 off several electric vehicles for Black Friday, including the three-row EV9 and the Niro EV.\nThe 2026 Kia EV9 is available with a $10,000 Customer Cash discount that can be applied toward the purchase price. With a $10,000 discount, prices for the base EV9 Light RWD trim can fall to as low as $44,900 ($54,900 starting MSRP).\n2026 Kia EV9 (Source: Kia)\nKia is also promoting a lease deal on the 2026 EV9 Light Long Range RWD for $339/month for 36 months, with $4,999 due at signing.\nIf you opt to finance, you can get 0% APR for 60 months, plus $5,000 in APR Bonus Cash across the entire 2026 EV9 lineup.\nThe 2026 Kia Niro EV is also available with a $10,000 Customer Cash discount, knocking the price down to as low as $29,700 ($39,700 MSRP).\n2026 Kia Niro EV (Source: Kia)\nWith leases starting at just $289/month for 36 months (with $3,999 due at signing), the 2026 Niro EV Wind FWD is about as cheap a lease as you can get nowadays, gas or electric.\nThe Niro EV is also available with 0% APR for up to 72 months, including a $3,500 APR Bonus Cash discount.\nWhile it isn’t $10,000 off, it is worth mentioning that Kia now sells the smaller EV3 electric SUV. The 2027 Kia EV3 ( see our review ) starts at just $28,890, making it one of the most affordable EVs you can get in the US, alongside the new Chevy Bolt and Nissan LEAF.\n2027 Kia EV3 (Source: Kia)\nKia is offering a $1,500 Customer Cash discount on the 2027 EV3, which still makes it cheaper to buy outright than the Niro EV, even with incentives.\nThe 2027 Kia EV3 Wind FWD is available for lease starting at $349/month for 36 months, with $3,999 due at signing. Kia is offering 0.90% APR for 48 months on all 2027 EV3 trims.\nKia EV9 — See offers\nKia Niro EV — See offers\nKia EV3 — See offers\nKia’s current deals end on January 04, 2027.\nVolkswagen ID.4\nAs it prepares to introduce its replacement in 2027, Volkswagen introduced a $10,000 Customer Bonus for the 2026 ID.4 electric SUV.\n2026 Volkswagen ID.4 (Source: Volkswagen)\nSince the ID.4 is discontinued after the 2026 model year, it might not be so easy to find one. Volkswagen said the remaining inventory is very limited.\nIf you can find one, Volkswagen will apply the $10,000 discount when you purchase or lease a new 2026 ID.4 through a participating dealer.\nVolkswagen ID.4 — See offers\nVolkswagen’s current ID.4 offer runs until November 30, 2026. You can read more about its replacement, the ID. Tiguan here .\nOther Black Friday EV deals worth a look\nWith the new 2027 models arriving, automakers are offering generous discounts and other financing deals on 2026 models to clear inventory.\nThrough its annual Winter Getaway sales event, Hyundai is offering up to $7,000 off the three-row 2026 IONIQ 9 or leases starting at just $419 a month. The offer is a 36-month lease for the IONIQ 9 S RWD trim with $4,999 due at signing.\n2026 Hyundai IONIQ 9 (Source: Hyundai)\nPrefer something smaller? The 2026 Hyundai IONIQ 5 is available with up to a $3,500 discount. Leases start at just $339 a month (24 months with $4,999 due at signing) for the standard-range IONIQ SE RWD, or $349 a month (24 months with $4,999 due at signing) for the standard-range IONIQ SE RWD.\nHyundai’s Winter Getaway sales event runs through November 30.\nHyundai IONIQ 5 — See offers\nHyundai IONIQ 9 — See offers\nToyota is currently offering a deal on the 2026 bZ Woodland , its bigger, more rugged electric SUV for Black Friday that’s worth checking out.\nThe deal includes 0% APR financing for 72 months, plus an extra $1,000 Holiday Bonus Cash. Toyota said that if you finance a new 2026 bZ Woodland for 72 payments, it will cost $13.89 for every $1,000 financed.\nToyota bZ Woodland Premium (Source: Toyota)\nTop comment by Douglas Brown\nLiked by 5 people\nIs this article simply an advert for these brands? When you click for 'see offers' it demands your email and phone number. Forget it!\nView all comments\nIn comparison, the standard 2026 bZ is available with 1.99% interest for 72 months at $14.75 for every $1,000 financed.\nThe standard 2026 Toyota bZ is available to lease, starting at $369 per month. The deal is for a 36-month lease with $4,369 due at signing for an effective cost of $490 per month.\nToyota is promoting 2026 bZ Woodland leases as low as $449 a month. That’s also for a 36-month lease with $4,448 due at signing.\nToyota’s current offers also end on November 30.\nToyota bZ — See offers\nToyota bZ Woodland — See offers\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
